---
// Privacy: the essays' page. The same column structure (a label column, then the text),
// the same type and hairlines, so it reads as one family with Writing and About.
// Every sentence and link is as it was; only the layout changed.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/privacy.css';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Shannon Hecker" description="How this site uses optional analytics, the game scoreboard and the Ask Shannon chat, and how to change your choice.">
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="privacy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="privacy-head">
        <p class="privacy-eyebrow">Privacy · 19 November 2026</p>
        <h1>Your visit, your choice.</h1>
      </header>
      <div class="privacy-body">
        <section class="privacy-sec" aria-labelledby="privacy-analytics">
          <h2 id="privacy-analytics">Optional analytics</h2>
          <div class="privacy-text">
            <p>Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity load only when you choose “Allow analytics”. I use their private reports to understand visits, reading depth and which game stages people play.</p>
            <p>Google Analytics uses cookies and device and browser information to distinguish visits. Advertising features are off. I exclude nicknames, form entries and query strings. Clarity records clicks and scrolling for heatmaps and session replays. Text inputs, the scoreboard and Ask Shannon are masked. Clarity can capture query strings in page addresses.</p>
            <p>Your choice lasts six months on this browser. Change it in <button type="button" class="privacy-inline" data-analytics-settings>Analytics settings</button>. Declining keeps the site and game available, stops both tools and clears their site cookies. The page reloads if Clarity was running. I cannot clear cookies Microsoft sets on its own domains.</p>
            <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy<span class="vh"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> · <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft’s privacy statement<span class="vh"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="privacy-sec" aria-labelledby="privacy-chat">
          <h2 id="privacy-chat">Ask Shannon chat</h2>
          <div class="privacy-text">
            <p>My private chat server sends your message to Anthropic to generate a reply. I keep chat logs for up to 30 days.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="privacy-sec" aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
          <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact and sales</h2>
          <div class="privacy-text">
            <p>I use your email address and message only to reply. I do not sell personal information.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="privacy-sec" aria-labelledby="privacy-game">
          <h2 id="privacy-game">The game scoreboard</h2>
          <div class="privacy-text">
            <p>Completed stages and mission stars stay in browser storage on this device. Clearing site data resets your progress.</p>
            <p>Sharing a score is optional. If you choose to share, your score and optional nickname appear on the public stage scoreboard. Please choose a made-up name.</p>
            <p>Vercel and Upstash process scoreboard data. Each stage stores up to 100 results and shows the best ten. Run receipts expire after two hours. To limit spam, a keyed address digest expires after one hour. The scoreboard database does not store raw addresses.</p>
            <p>To remove a score, send me the stage, nickname and score on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shannonhecker/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn<span class="vh"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
